    "blind_description": "Black-line corner perspective drawing on white:\n- A two-face corner building, complete outer rectangular wall outlines meeting at a thick vertical corner edge, resting on a horizontal ground line.\n- Two matching rectangular signs wrap the corner, each containing hand-drawn legible text “CAFÉ”; the É accents are short separate marks.\n- Below the signs, a continuous corner awning/signboard with vertical panel division lines and small J-shaped end marks; its lower edge is a wavy scalloped line on both faces.\n- Under it on each facade is a large window: complete outer rectangles, one horizontal and one vertical crossbar dividing each into four panes, plus a thin lower sill strip.\n- At the corner, a narrow door is drawn as a vertical rectangle overlapping the corner line, with one small horizontal handle mark; its full depth/thickness is partially indicated.\n- Foreground sidewalk/patio has two fully drawn small round pedestal tables: circular tops with internal radial lines, straight stems, T-shaped bases. Faint thin perspective paving lines are visible. No chairs or people are drawn.",
